  {
    "sha": "4eaae03d4a21c4312bd85fb55e67b57149b04bb7",
    "node_id": "C_kwDONSoFw9oAKDRlYWFlMDNkNGEyMWM0MzEyYmQ4NWZiNTVlNjdiNTcxNDliMDRiYjc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Alvin Chang",
        "email": "alvinga@andestech.com",
        "date": "2026-02-23T03:27:47Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Alvin Chang",
        "email": "alvinga@andestech.com",
        "date": "2026-02-24T02:51:47Z"
      },
      "message": "Reference Model: Add rridscp_unselectable configuration for RRIDSCP\n\nThe IOPMP specification says that it is unnecessary to allow every\nimplemented RRID to be selectable by RRIDSCP.rrid field. To allow users\nto configure whether the implemented RRID is selectable or unselectable,\nwe add rridscp_unselectable signals as part of the configurations of the\nreference model. By setting rridscp_unselectable[RRID]=1, the RRID\nbecomes unselectable.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "8cd5980e7494fb21291af4b7306fc5e607dd9e87",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv-non-isa/riscv-iopmp/git/trees/8cd5980e7494fb21291af4b7306fc5e607dd9e87"
      },
